{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_eisenstein_norm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_eisenstein_norm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branch_subtree_no_oddPreimage","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branch_subtree_no_oddPreimage","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L273-L299","doc":"**The tree-structure theorem.** Let `p = branchEval w k` be the evaluation at\nthe odd-preimage node of the `k`-th branch, `k ≥ 1`. Then **no** node of the even\nsubtree above it admits an odd-preimage:\n\n    ∀ n, ¬ ∃ Q, [2]_q·(αⁿ·p) = [3]_q·Q + 1.\n\nSo each `k ≥ 1` branch of the backward tree is a **bare even chain** — it\ncarries no second odd step. Together with the main chain (`k = 0`, which returns\nto the attractor) this exhausts the tree: every node lies on the main chain or on\na bare `k ≥ 1` branch, and **no two odd-preimages ever chain**.\n\nConsequence for the arc: no `v = 0` block occurs in the backward tree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branchEval_not_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branchEval_not_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L250-L271","doc":"**The branch evaluation is not a unit, for every `k ≥ 1`.**\n\nThis is the missing arithmetic input to the unit-obstruction engine\n`CollatzBlockDescent.evenSubtree_no_oddPreimage`: the engine shows that a\nnon-unit evaluation blocks odd-preimages through the entire even subtree, but\ndoes not itself establish that the `k ≥ 1` branch evaluations are non-units.\nThe Eisenstein norm supplies exactly that. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eisNorm_dvd_one_of_mul_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eisNorm_dvd_one_of_mul_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L229-L248","doc":"**Norm-`1` is necessary for a unit.** If `eis w x y` is a unit whose inverse\nalso has integral coordinates, the norm form takes the value `±1`.\n\nStated in the form actually used: a factorisation of `1` in Eisenstein\ncoordinates forces `N(x,y)` to divide `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branch_norm_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branch_norm_ge","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L218-L225","doc":"The branch norm is at least `19` once `k ≥ 1` — the first branch already\nmisses `1` by a wide margin, which is why the obstruction is structural rather\nthan marginal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branch_norm_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branch_norm_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L206-L216","doc":"**The norm is `1` only on the main chain.** For `k ≥ 1` the branch norm\nexceeds `1`, so the branch evaluation is not a unit of `ℤ[ω]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branch_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branch_norm","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L196-L204","doc":"**The branch-norm formula.** The odd-preimage taken at the `n = 6k` node of\nthe main even chain lands on an evaluation of Eisenstein norm\n\n    N(Q_k(w)) = 1 + 6k + 12k².\n\nPure arithmetic in `ℤ` on the coordinates `(-(4k+1), -(2k+1))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branch_deriv_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branch_deriv_relation","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L182-L192","doc":"**The derivative relation at the branch node.** The odd-preimage evaluation\n`branchEval w k` satisfies `(2w + 1)·Q(w) = P(w) + (w+1)·P'(w)` with\n`P(w) = chainEval w` and `P'(w) = chainDeriv w k`.\n\nThis is the identity the probe verifies numerically; here it is a `ring`\nidentity modulo `w² + w + 1 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainData_at_six_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainData_at_six_mul","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L165-L180","doc":"**The main chain has the right data at `n = 6k`.** With `u₀ = v₀ = -w`,\nthe closed form `chainData_snd` reproduces `chainDeriv` at `n = 6k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branchEval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.branchEval","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L161-L163","doc":"The evaluation of the odd-preimage taken at the `n = 6k` node,\n`-(4k+1) - (2k+1)·w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainDeriv","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L157-L159","doc":"The derivative at the `n = 6k` node of the main even chain,\n`-6k - (6k+1)·w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainEval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainEval","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L154-L155","doc":"The evaluation at the `n = 6k` node of the main even chain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainData_snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainData_snd","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L130-L142","doc":"**The closed form for the derivative**, `α·v_n = α^(n+1)·v₀ + n·αⁿ·u₀`.\nMultiplying by the unit `α` clears the `αⁿ⁻¹`, so this holds over any\n`CommRing` with no invertibility side condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainData_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainData_fst","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L122-L128","doc":"The evaluation half is a pure geometric progression: `u_n = αⁿ·u₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainData_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainData_succ","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L117-L120","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainData_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainData_zero","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L115-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.chainData","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L109-L113","doc":"The chain data after `n` even branch-inverses, as an explicit pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.alpha_pow_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.alpha_pow_six","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L96-L102","doc":"**`α = w + 1` has multiplicative order dividing 6** — this is the source of\nthe `6` in the observed mod-6 congruence along the main even chain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.alpha_pow_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.alpha_pow_three","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L92-L94","doc":"`(w + 1)³ = -1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eisNorm_alpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eisNorm_alpha","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L89-L90","doc":"`N(α) = 1`: the even branch-inverse is norm-preserving. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eis_alpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eis_alpha","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L86-L87","doc":"`α = w + 1` in Eisenstein coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eis_mul_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eis_mul_conj","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L76-L82","doc":"The Eisenstein conjugate of `x + y·w` is `(x - y) - y·w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eisNorm_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eisNorm_mul","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L70-L74","doc":"The norm form is multiplicative — a pure identity in `ℤ`, matching\n`eis_mul`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eis_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eis_mul","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L64-L68","doc":"Multiplication in Eisenstein coordinates. Uses `w² = -1 - w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eis_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eis_one","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eis_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eis_zero","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eisNorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eisNorm","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L57-L58","doc":"The integral norm form `N(x + y·w) = x² - xy + y²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzEisenstein.eis","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_eisenstein_norm.lean#L53-L55","doc":"`eis x y = x + y·w`, the element of `R` with Eisenstein coordinates\n`(x, y)` relative to the cube root `w`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}